  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through next Thursday) \nIssued at 1151 AM CDT Thu Sep 24 2026\n\nExpect mainly an upper level southwest flow pattern through late \nthis week and then ridging returning this weekend and a stronger \nupper level trough next week which will increase rain chances. The \nbetter lift and tropical moisture will still remain to our west \nFriday and Saturday with only a few showers and thunderstorms \npossible across our area, mainly north and west(low chance). \nOtherwise. a dry forecast this weekend. A more unsettled pattern \nwith increasing tropical moisture(PW values 1.5 to 2 inches), an \nupper level storm system and cold front will result in low-medium\nchances of rain(scattered showers and thunderstorms) early to \nmiddle of next week. Localize rainfall amounts of greater than 1 \ninch are possible across much of the area. Temperatures will \nremain above normal this weekend and then cooler temperatures \nmiddle of next week, highs in the 80s.",
